  "correction_rules": [
    "When sentiment history shows a sustained positive trend (e.g., >0.50 over multiple days), model forecasts tend to overestimate prices; reduce forecast by 5-10% in such regimes.",
    "After a sharp price spike (e.g., >10% from prior day), model often overshoots; apply a 1-2 day lag correction by lowering forecast by 5-15% for the next 2-3 days.",
    "If model consistently forecasts below true outcome in a range (e.g., 65-75), consider mean reversion bias — adjust forecast upward by 2-5% for next 3-5 days.",
    "In low sentiment (sentiment < 0.00 for 3+ days), model underestimates; increase forecast by 3-8% for next 2-4 days to capture potential rebound.",
    "For horizon > 30d, model tends to overfit recent trends; apply smoothing filter (e.g., 3-day moving average) to reduce volatility amplification.",
    "When true outcome deviates >10% from 30d forecast, check sentiment history — if sentiment is neutral or negative, model may be underreacting; adjust upward by 5-10%."
  ]
}
